-- THE CHANGE LOCATION SETUP (canon 0.30.40). Owner, 2026-09-11, verbatim in the
-- canon row: "Create the "Change Location" setup" with the toggle, the farm, the
-- license, the package, to/from, the seed locations, an Execute button, a
-- warning, and "All movements are within the license itself, so the CSV is for
-- a location change, not a transfer manifest."
--
-- Locations now know their license: license_value NULL means every license at
-- the farm (a Barn, the Blast Freezer at PNN); a set value scopes the row to
-- one line (the processor's rooms, racks and stations under AU-P-000694; each
-- license's own field rows and greenhouses). The existing rows keep their
-- meaning: BARN (PNN, all licenses), ARL BARN, PNS BARN; CSB becomes the
-- processor's. Field locations (plants) are seeded per license exactly as
-- METRC names them in his exports of 2026-09-11 ("List the rows and GHs that
-- you see from the reports"), plus Barn at every farm. Inventory locations
-- (packages) follow his list. The rack grid is 12 sides (6 racks, two sides
-- each) x 4 stanchion bays x 4 levels a to d, coded side.bay.level (1.3.c),
-- 192 slots; his own example's words are read as side 1, bay 3, level c.
-- location_changes records every move (one group per Execute) so the METRC
-- Location Change file pends on /admin/uploads, one export home.

ALTER TABLE lookup_values ADD COLUMN license_value TEXT;

UPDATE lookup_values SET license_value = 'AU-P-000694'
WHERE category = 'inventory_location' AND value = 'CSB' AND deleted_at IS NULL;

-- Inventory locations (packages): his list.
